> 1> 2 Bones levels without gravestones. Level 5 had ghost and stack of
> equipment.  Third level Mine had stack of equipment no ghost, no stone.
> (I have never noticed this before)

Characters who are turned to stone do not leave ghosts.  It's also
possible that, since they can go through walls, the ghost left the
scene looking for you, and you just never saw him or mistook him for a
dark spot.


> 2> My God Set will not give me any artifacts, hell he won't give me
> anything.  I have run through 3 wands of create monster, about 30
> charges, 5 or 6 blessed scrolls of CM and have sacrificed 3 white
> unicorns and 2 grey unicorns numerous ants/bees/rothe/cubes/giants
> /leprechauns(2 halls worth) and even 7 or 8 black puddings. And have
> recieved nothing but four leaf clovers. I haven't killed anything I
> shouldn't have and have prayed once, as soon as I found the altar to
> make holy water, before all this sacrificing. Whats going on?

Your god's generosity always has a significant random component.  Plus,
if there has already been a couple of artifacts generated in your game,
it'll be harder to get one from your deity.  But it's possible to miss
out just by being unlucky.  (And maybe from having low luck.)


> 3> Since the first level where I ran into 2 rust traps which rusted my
> axe, I been wielding an Elven Broadsword and Elven Bow.  Neither skill
> has risen.

You may have used up all the equipment slots you've earned so far on
other weapons.


> 4> For killing 3 rothe I used a blessed aklys and my Club skill
> rose...Shouldn't that be a dagger skill?

If you gained a level from killing the rothe, then you'd get an
additional skill slot.  (It would not automatically advance you in Club
though, you'd have to do that yourself.)  If you had been level-drained
before and lost a slot from that, you would get it back by regaining
that level, but again I think it'd be returned to you unassigned.


> 5> No shops through 16 levels except for mine town which had armor,
> light and hardware. Lots of altars all chaotic. (Six I think)

Interesting.  Note that shops get rarer the deeper you go.  (Levels two
and three always have a shop if there's an eligable room -- that's one
with one exit and no stairs -- on those levels.)


